# UC-07 Order Tracking

## Use Case ID
UC-07

## Use Case Name
Order Tracking

## Description
This use case describes how a customer tracks the current status of an order using the Order ID.

## Primary Actor
Customer

## Secondary Actor
None

## Preconditions
- Customer has a successfully placed order.
- Customer has a valid Order ID.

## Trigger
Customer wants to check the current status of an order.

## Main Flow
1. Customer navigates to the **Tracking** section.
2. Customer enters the Order ID.
3. Customer submits the Order ID.
4. System validates the Order ID.
5. System retrieves the corresponding order details.
6. System displays the current order status.
7. Customer views the applicable status, such as **Processing, Shipped, Out for Delivery, or Delivered**.

## Alternate Flow

### A1: Invalid Order ID
1. Customer enters an invalid Order ID.
2. System cannot find the corresponding order.
3. System displays an appropriate message.
4. Customer enters the correct Order ID.

## Postconditions
- Customer can view the current status of the order.
- Customer can monitor the order until delivery is completed.

## Business Rules
- Customer must provide a valid Order ID to track an order.
- System must display the latest available order status.